"Students should know heat engines, efficiency and the Carnot efficiency, and ideally have met S = Q/T for a reservoir. The demo has three views. <strong>Free expansion</strong>: hard disks in a box {#} by {#} units start in the left half behind a partition; the count on the left and a histogram of time spent at each count are shown once the partition is removed. <strong>Einstein solids</strong>: two solids of N_A and N_B oscillators share q quanta by random exchanges of one quantum at a time; Ω_A Ω_B is plotted against q_A. <strong>Second law</strong>: an engine or refrigerator between two reservoirs, with ΔS of each reservoir and of the universe, and a pairing with a Carnot partner.",
